From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] serial: pl01x: support the PL011 AXI compatible

Linux 6.12 Raspberry Pi device trees describe the BCM2712 PL011 using
the arm,pl011-axi compatible. Recognise it as a standard PL011 so that
U-Boot can continue to use the SoC debug UART on Raspberry Pi 5 and
Compute Module 5.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c b/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c
index 0389b26963..ed15efe226 100644
--- a/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@ static const struct dm_serial_ops pl01x_serial_ops = {
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_REAL)
 static const struct udevice_id pl01x_serial_id[] ={
 	{.compatible = "arm,pl011", .data = TYPE_PL011},
+	{.compatible = "arm,pl011-axi", .data = TYPE_PL011},
 	{.compatible = "arm,pl010", .data = TYPE_PL010},
 	{}
 };
